# AGENTS.md — @@PROJECT@@ GitOps Repository

> **AI agents:** Read this file before working in this repository. It describes the layout, CI/CD patterns, and Emerald OpenShift conventions used here.

## Repository purpose

This repo deploys **@@PROJECT@@** to the BC Government OpenShift Emerald cluster using `ag-helm-templates` and the four-tool policy-as-code gate.

## Directory layout

```text
.github/
  workflows/
    ci.yml          <- triggers .NET CI workflows
    cd.yml          <- GitOps deploy workflow (per environment)
  CODEOWNERS        <- PR approval rules
gitops/
  Chart.yaml        <- Helm umbrella chart (depends on ag-helm-templates)
  values.yaml       <- shared values (all components)
  values-dev.yaml   <- dev environment overrides
  values-test.yaml  <- test environment overrides
  values-prod.yaml  <- prod environment overrides
  templates/        <- generated by scaffold.py (ag-helm fragments)
Makefile            <- shortcuts: make render, make lint, make validate
```

## How to add a new component

1. Generate manifests with the `deploying-bc-gov-workloads` skill (`scripts/scaffold.py --type <deployment|service|route|networkpolicy> --name <component>`).
2. Files are written to `gitops/templates/<component>-<kind>.yaml`.
3. Add component values to `gitops/values.yaml` and `values-{dev,test,prod}.yaml`.

## CI/CD

- **CI:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs dependency restore, build, lint, and tests.
- **CD:** `.github/workflows/cd.yml` runs `helm template` + four-tool policy validation + `helm upgrade` per environment on merge to `main`.
- **Secrets required:** `OPENSHIFT_SERVER`, `OPENSHIFT_TOKEN` (per environment in GitHub Environments).

## Policy validation

Before pushing, validate rendered manifests:

```bash
make render       # helm template gitops/ > rendered.yaml
make validate     # runs datree + polaris + kube-linter + conftest
```

## Key constraints

- All Deployments must set `DataClass: Low|Medium|High` (default `Medium` for VIPs; `dataclass-low` has no VIP on Emerald).
- Every component must have a matching NetworkPolicy — no open ingress/egress.
- Routes must use `edge` TLS termination (frontends or approved exceptions only).
- AVI annotation (`aviinfrasetting.ako.vmware.com/name`) is required on all Route and Ingress resources.
